1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,067
Rule six. Never sleep in a bed they
made for you. Your clothes, your
blanket, your own door.

2
00:00:06,567 --> 00:00:12,333
A motel, with one room open. Fresh
sheets. A chocolate on the pillow. It
is so quiet. It is so soft.

3
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:18,800
Beds with the covers turned down, in
the window of every shop. Pillows for
people who haven't arrived yet.

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:24,300
You sit on the floor with your back
against the door. And the warm smell
finds you anyway.

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:32,333
Your eyelids get heavy. Your thoughts
get smooth. You forget why you came.
You forget the bus. You forget Sam.
And then you cough.

6
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:39,367
Your lungs tighten. The air is thick
and sweet. It burns. For the first
time in your life, you are glad you're
sick.

7
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:44,867
The smoke makes everyone calm. It
makes me cough. And a cough keeps you
awake.

8
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:50,500
Rule seven. Never trust a calm you
didn't choose. If you feel too good,
ask why.
